# Next.js + ShadCN Guidelines

## General Best Practices

- Only use [Next.js-recommended APIs](https://nextjs.org/docs) and ShadCN-approved patterns.
- Prefer [App Router](https://nextjs.org/docs/app) conventions (app directory, layouts, loading, etc.).
- Keep pages and components as small and modular as possible.
- Place page-level components in `/app`; place UI and utility components in `/components`.

## Routing & Navigation

- Use `<Link>` from `next/link` for client-side navigation. Do **not** use `<a>` directly for internal links.
- Use `href` with absolute or root-relative URLs.

## Data Fetching

- Use [server components](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/rendering/server-components) for data fetching when possible.
- Use [Next.js caching and revalidation](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/data-fetching/caching) (e.g. `fetch`, `revalidate`).

## Styling

- Always use [ShadCN UI primitives](https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components) where a suitable component exists.
- Use Tailwind CSS for custom styling.
- Never override ShadCN or Tailwind base classNames without good reason.

## Accessibility (a11y)

- ShadCN UI components are accessible out of the box. Keep overrides minimal and test accessibility if you customize.
- Always provide meaningful `alt` prop for images, and don’t use "image" or "photo" in the alt text.
- Use appropriate semantic elements and heading structures.

## Component Usage

- Only use UI elements from ShadCN (or Next's built-ins) for buttons, forms, cards, alerts, dialogs, etc.
- Never copy raw HTML from the ShadCN docs—import components from your `/components/ui/` directory instead.
- Compose new components by reusing ShadCN UI where possible.

## State & Behavior

- Use React server components by default.
- Use client components (with `'use client'`) only for interactive UI (input, dialogs, drag, etc.).
- Store transient UI state (modals, toggles) in local component state, not global state (except as required).

## Imports & Exports

- Always use named exports for components and utility functions.
- Use absolute imports based on your project’s tsconfig or jsconfig paths.

## Image Usage

- Always use `<Image>` from `next/image` for rendering images. Never use `<img>`.
- Use the `alt` prop and specify `sizes` and `priority` where appropriate.

## External Links

- Use `target="_blank"` together with `rel="noopener noreferrer"` for external links.
- Only use `<a>` for true external URLs.

## Miscellaneous

- Do **not** use Next.js `<head>` or import `next/head` outside of allowed locations (`_document.tsx`, root `layout.tsx`).
- Do **not** use `any` or `unknown` types.
- Validate all props using TypeScript and prefer explicit typing.

## File Organization

- Place each UI component or utility in its own file within the `/components/ui/` or `/components/` directory.
- Do **not** place logic or UI inside API route files.

# ShadCN-specific rules

- Do **not** modify core ShadCN component source—extend via composition or props.
- Update ShadCN components via the CLI, not by editing generated code directly.
- Follow ShadCN’s accessibility and keyboard navigation guidelines for customizations.

# Next.js-specific rules

- Do **not** use `<img>` or `<head>` HTML elements. Use Next.js’ `<Image>` and layout/head conventions.
- Always prefer static rendering (SSG/ISR) unless SSR is required.
- Do **not** use global CSS except for built-in Tailwind/base styles.

# Errors & Edge Cases

- Always handle async errors using try/catch in server functions and edge logic.
- Use user-friendly default/fallback content for missing props, missing images, etc.

